{number: 92}
{title: Saviour, Like a Shepherd Lead Us}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Savior, like a shepherd lead us,
Much we need Thy [G7] tender care;
In Thy [C] pleasant pastures feed us,
For our use Thy [G7] folds pre-[C] pare:
Blessed [F] Jesus, blessed [C] Jesus,
Thou hast [G7] bought us, Thine we [C] are;
Blessed [F] Jesus, blessed [C] Jesus,
Thou hast [G7] bought us, Thine we [C] are.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] We are Thine, do Thou befriend us,
Be the Guardian [G7] of our way;
Keep Thy [C] flock, from sin defend us,
Seek us when we [G7] go a-[C] stray:
Blessed [F] Jesus, blessed [C] Jesus,
Hear, O [G7] hear us when we [C] pray;
Blessed [F] Jesus, blessed [C] Jesus,
Hear, O [G7] hear us when we [C] pray.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Thou hast promised to receive us,
Poor and sinful [G7] though we be;
Thou hast [C] mercy to relieve us,
Grace to cleanse, and [G7] pow'r to [C] free:
Blessed [F] Jesus, blessed [C] Jesus,
Early [G7] let us turn to [C] Thee;
Blessed [F] Jesus, blessed [C] Jesus,
Early [G7] let us turn to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
